From: Halcyon Browser Project <halcyon@local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] browser_view: Use HalcyonTabStrip

Replaces the upstream TabStrip with HalcyonTabStrip. The HalcyonTabStrip
visually differentiates from upstream by:

  - flat (no rounded corners) tabs
  - active tab background matches the page background (the active tab
    visually IS the page)
  - anchored tabs visually distinct and group-at-start
  - no tab search button
  - new-tab button as a single small "+" at the right edge

The upstream TabStrip class is left in place; Halcyon doesn't instantiate
it. The HalcyonTabStripController (a small class in
chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/halcyon_tab_strip_controller.h) bridges to
the upstream TabStripModel so all the model-side logic (session restore,
tab selection, etc.) is unchanged.

---
 chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
@@ -49,6 +49,8 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/tab_strip.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/halcyon_tab_strip.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/halcyon_tab_strip_controller.h"

@@ -440,8 +442,16 @@ void BrowserView::InitBrowserView() {
   ...
-  tabstrip_ = AddChildView(std::make_unique<TabStrip>(tabstrip_controller));
+  if (base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(features::kHalcyonUI)) {
+    halcyon_tabstrip_controller_ =
+        std::make_unique<HalcyonTabStripController>(browser());
+    halcyon_tabstrip_ = AddChildView(
+        std::make_unique<halcyon::HalcyonTabStrip>(halcyon_tabstrip_controller_.get()));
+    tabstrip_ = halcyon_tabstrip_;
+  } else {
+    tabstrip_ = AddChildView(std::make_unique<TabStrip>(tabstrip_controller));
+  }
   ...
 }
